# Server event emit

Emit through Auth (`userEmit`, `batchUserEmit`, `organizationEmit`, `emitServerEvent`) when work finishes **off the request** that started it. Typical case: a Workflow job. The UI will not get a completion payload, so SSE tells it to refetch or patch cache.

The acting User already receives the mutation result. They do not need an SSE for that write.

## Emit from

- Workflow job `.handle` after the job creates or updates a resource
- Other background work the User did not wait on (cron, inbound callback that persisted something)

```typescript
.handle(async (payload) => {
  // ... job work ...
  this.service.auth.userEmit({
    userId: payload.userId,
    resource: "workflow",
    id: jobName,
    change: "updated",
    organizationId: null,
  });
});
```

Call Auth directly. Do not wrap `userEmit` in a private helper that only forwards.

## Organization fan-out

`organizationEmit` (or `emitServerEvent` with an Organization id) notifies **other Members**. Use it when those Members must see a change they did not make — a job created an org-scoped entity, a publish, an assignment. Skip it for routine field edits.

## Client

Mount `ServerEventProvider` in the app shell. Register a handler that invalidates the matching `queryFilter()`. Reconnect has no replay: `onReconnect` should invalidate the same queries. Keep polling only as a fallback for in-progress status (queued → running) if you emit only when the job finishes.

Starter: `DemoWorkflowService` `demo.ping` + `trpc.workflow.list`.
